<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13180" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-pĭlo</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a.
			id., <i>to pull out the hair, pluck out
				the feathers</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Prop. (ante-class. and post-Aug., and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">depilari magis quam amiciri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perdicem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Apic. 6,
					3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Mart. 9, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">struthiocamelum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. Sap. 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amygdalae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Apic. 2,
					2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>,
			dēpĭlātus, <i>plucked</i>, i. e. <i>plundered, cheated</i>, Lucil.
			ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 36,
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To rub off the skin, peel</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnis umerus depilatus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Ezech. 29, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
